#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128930 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129117 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "2b2f2b8e-4625-5550-bb37-5ab9ca409c50" :question/math-academy-id "e-5032" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{2x+20}[/math]}} \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{20x+25}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+20 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20x+25 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are $2x+20$ and $20x+25.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128931 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129118 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "bda2e91a-5b55-5deb-8232-7e79fabf6f29" :question/math-academy-id "e-5033" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]}} \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128933 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "e3e171d1-4428-5a4d-a050-5ad8eb843aff" :question/math-academy-id "e-5110" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, what is $\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5}?$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $2x^2+8x -5$ by the linear binomial ${\\color{purple}x+5}$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${\\color{blue}2x-2},$ and\n\n- the remainder ${\\color{red}5}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5} = {\\color{blue}2x-2}+\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{purple}x+5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129118 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6409232-2d31-593b-90bb-8a5813883aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+48\\,$ and $\\,48x-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399825} {:answer/id #uuid "8add39dc-99a4-5ff4-9055-09c5f3363d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-24\\,$ and $\\,24x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399826} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8cd1cd-1378-56d5-a7ab-7daa3b9b05fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+30\\,$ and $\\,30x-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399827} {:answer/id #uuid "29edcf41-1ad2-52f3-ab8d-9b28e983225b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-36\\,$ and $\\,48x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399828} {:answer/id #uuid "f2683559-249d-5d23-9f72-d0c8764dba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2683559-249d-5d23-9f72-d0c8764dba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399829} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb0dafe-c8dd-5892-9eb8-f305e87ca008" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3536c096-9c19-5ecb-8cd6-bf3a33c8475e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114262" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows: \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-4\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+36 \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,36x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4.$"}]}
